.\" jb.1 — manual page for jb
.\"
.TH JB 1 "August 9, 2026" "jb 0.1" "General Commands Manual"
.
.SH NAME
jb \- a git-inspired agentic coding loop (pi-compatible sessions)
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jb
.B init
.br
.B jb
.B run
.RI [ \-\-fork\~ID ]
.RI [ \-c\~KEY=VALUE ]
.br
.B jb
.B commit
.I ID
.RI [ \-m\~subject ]
.RI [ \-m\~body ]
.br
.B jb
.BR status " | " log
.RI [ \-\-graph ]
.RB "| " show
.RI [ ID ]
.RB "| " ps
.RB "| " wait
.I ID
.RB "| " path
.I ID
.RB "| " export
.I ID
.RI [ PATH ]
.RB "| " config
.RI [ \-\-global | \-\-local ]
.RI [ KEY [ VALUE ]]
.RB "| " help
.RI [ VERB ]
.br
.B jb
.BR \-C\~DIR " | " \-c\~KEY=VALUE
...
.br
.B jb
.B \-\-version
.br
.B jb
.B \-\-help
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jb
is a minimal agentic coding loop: a single C binary that reads a prompt
from standard input, sends it to an OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions
API, executes any tool calls the model requests in a loop, and prints the
model's final answer to standard output.
.PP
.B jb
borrows git's workflow shape.  Each project has a repository (a plain
.B .jb/
directory created by
.BR "jb init" ) ;
sessions live under
.BR .jb/sessions/<uuid>/ .
A session runs
.RI ( status "working" ),
finishes
.RI ( "completed" ),
and only an explicit
.B jb commit
finalizes it
.RI ( "committed" ).
Cleanup is the filesystem: there is no
.BR "jb rm" .
.PP
The conversation is stored in the pi session format
.RB ( session.jsonl ,
JSONL v3) \(em the same format the pi coding agent uses \(em so pi's
viewers and exporters render jb sessions unchanged.  The OpenAI wire shape
is derived from that file at request time and never stored.
.B jb export
produces the pi viewer HTML (template embedded in the binary) or the
linear JSONL.
.
.SS Repository
.B jb init
creates
.B .jb/
containing
.B config.json
(the local config) and
.BR sessions/ .
Commands resolve the repository by walking up from the current directory;
outside any repository jb prints
.RI ( "jb: fatal: not a jb repository (run 'jb init')" )
and exits 1.
.B \-C\~DIR
resolves the repository from
.I DIR
instead of the current directory.
.
.SS Sessions
Each
.B jb run
creates
.B .jb/sessions/<uuid>/
containing:
.TP
.B session.jsonl
The authoritative conversation \(em pi session format v3: a header line
followed by one entry per message, each with an 8-hex id, parentId chain,
ISO-ms timestamp, role, content blocks, usage, and stopReason.
.TP
.B events.jsonl
The live stream \(em pi json-mode events, delta-only.  First line is the
session header; then agent_start, message_start/update/end (updates carry
only deltas), tool_execution_start/end, and agent_end.
.TP
.B metadata.json
The jb index: uuid, subject, body, author, parent, status, started_at,
ended_at, working_dir, config snapshot, turns, tokens_used, exit_code,
last_activity.  Written atomically at init and close; rewritten by
.BR "jb commit" .
.PP
Sessions are single-branch: every entry's parentId is the previous entry's
id.  The first entry's parentId is null.  All metadata writes are atomic
(temp file + rename); readers never see a partial file.
.
.SS ID resolution
Session IDs may be given as the full uuid, a unique prefix of at least 4
hex characters, or
.B @
for
.BR $JB_SESSION .
Errors: \(oqjb: no session \(cqxyz\(cq\(cq, \(oqjb: ambiguous id
\(cqabc1\(cq (abc123\&..., abc1de\&...)\(cq, \(oqjb: JB_SESSION not
set\(cq \(em all exit 1.
.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B jb init
Create
.B .jb/
with
.B sessions/
and an empty local
.BR config.json .
Idempotent \(em a second run prints \(oqreinitialized\(cq.
.TP
.B jb run [\-\-fork ID] [\-c KEY=VALUE]
Read the prompt from standard input (required; \(oqjb: no prompt on
stdin\(cq, exit 2), stream the model's answer to stdout, execute tool
calls in a loop, and record everything in the session files.  The session
uuid is exported as
.B JB_SESSION
for child processes.
.B \-\-fork
starts from a previous session's history (rebuilding the system prompt
fresh and trimming any dangling tail from an interrupted session).
.TP
.B jb commit ID [\-m subject] [\-m body]
Finalize a session: status must be completed or error (\(oqjb: session
\&... is working\(cq otherwise, exit 1), and an uncommitted parent is
refused.  The message comes from
.B \-m
or is auto-generated by the model (JSON-only completion).  Rewrites
metadata only \(em session.jsonl is never touched by a commit.  A
re-commit amends subject/body.
.TP
.B jb status
Git-status style view: the current session line (identity, status,
subject, age), its children, sessions awaiting commit, and the always-on
repo summary \(oqrepo: N sessions \&...\(cq.  A stale
.B JB_SESSION
prints a warning and falls back to the no-session view; exit 0.
.TP
.B jb log [\-\-graph]
Flat: id, status, author, age, subject, newest first.
.B \-\-graph
shows the committed forest only \(em roots oldest-first, children by
start time \(em with kinds root, fork, and fresh.
.TP
.B jb show [ID]
Pretty-print a session's metadata.json (indent 2); ID defaults to
.BR @ .
The metadata path is printed to stderr.
.TP
.B jb ps
List the children of the current session (sessions whose author is
.BR @ ),
then \(oqcommitted: N\(cq.  Exit 1 when
.B JB_SESSION
is not set.
.TP
.B jb wait ID
Poll a session's metadata.json every 250 ms until its status is completed
or error.  Exit 0 on completed, 1 on error/not-found.  Refuses the
current session (self-deadlock).
.TP
.B jb path ID
Print the session's directory \(em
.BR "tail -n 5 \"$(jb path ID)/session.jsonl\"" ,
.BR "jq . \"$(jb path ID)/metadata.json\"" .
.TP
.B jb export ID [PATH]
Export a session.  A
.B .jsonl
PATH is a byte-for-byte copy of session.jsonl (pi exportToJsonl shape,
directly importable).  Any other PATH (or no PATH) produces a
self-contained HTML viewer \(em the pi viewer template with the session
payload embedded.  The default filename is
.BR jb-session-<uuid>.html
in the current directory.  Working sessions may be exported (snapshot
semantics, no lock).  No gist upload \(em sharing is a manual
.BR "gh gist create\ \-\-public=false" .
.TP
.B jb config [\-\-global|\-\-local] [KEY [VALUE]]
Git-style configuration: list effective settings (local merged over
global), print one key, or set one.  Global file:
.BR ~/.config/jb/config.json ;
local file:
.BR .jb/config.json .
Any key is accepted and stored as a string, coerced at use.  Per-run
overrides use
.BR \-c\~KEY=VALUE .
.TP
.B jb help [VERB]
The command reference.  Bare
.B jb
is
.BR "jb help" .
.
.SS Global flags
.TP
.B \-C DIR
Resolve the repository from DIR (git \-C analog).
.TP
.B \-c KEY=VALUE
Config override (repeatable; meaningful for run).
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
Load config from PATH instead of the global file.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the command reference and exit 0.
.
.SS The Agentic Loop
Each
.I turn
consists of sending the full conversation (converted from the pi format
to the OpenAI wire shape) to the API, receiving a streaming response, and
acting on it:
.IP \(bu 3
If the model requests tool calls, jb executes them, feeds the results
back, and starts another turn.
.IP \(bu 3
If the model emits a final text message
.RI ( stopReason "stop"),
jb prints it to stdout and the session completes.
.IP \(bu 3
On API failure the session closes with status error; on SIGINT/SIGTERM
the assistant entry is recorded with stopReason aborted.
.PP
The system prompt is rebuilt fresh for every run and is never persisted;
forks do not inherit the parent's prompt snapshot.
.
.SS Tools
The model has access to five tools:
.TP
.BR read " \fIpath\fR [offset=\fIN\fR] [limit=\fIN\fR]"
Read file contents with line numbers.  Supports offset and limit for
large files.
.TP
.BR write " \fIpath\fR \fIcontent\fR"
Create or overwrite a file.  Creates parent directories as needed.
.TP
.BR edit " \fIpath\fR edits=[{oldText,newText},...]"
Make precise text replacements in a file.  Each edit must match a unique,
non-overlapping region.
.TP
.BR bash " \fIcommand\fR [timeout=\fIN\fR]"
Execute a shell command.  Output exceeding the configured limits is
saved to a temp file whose path is included in the tool result.
.TP
.BR jb " \fIprompt\fR [timeout=\fIN\fR]"
Spawn a child jb session to delegate a task.  The child inherits
.B JB_SESSION
and records the parent in its metadata \(em lineage is an observability
artifact, not a runtime dependency.
.
.SS Skills
A
.I skill
is a directory containing a
.B SKILL.md
file with YAML frontmatter
.RI ( name ","
description ) and a markdown body.
Skills are discovered from:
.IP \(bu 3
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jb/agents/skills/*/SKILL.md
\(em global skills
.IP \(bu 3
.B .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md
\(em project-local skills
.PP
An index of available skills is injected into the system prompt.
The model reads the full
.B SKILL.md
on demand via the
.B read
tool.
.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration comes from three sources, in increasing precedence: the
global file
.RB ( ~/.config/jb/config.json ,
or
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/jb/config.json
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is set), the local file
.RB ( .jb/config.json ),
and per-run
.B \-c
overrides.
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
    "api_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1",
    "model": "gpt-4.1",
    "max_tokens": 500000,
    "max_output_lines": 2000,
    "max_output_bytes": 51200
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
All fields are optional.  Defaults are shown above.  The effective
configuration is snapshotted into each session's metadata.json at run
time \(em the replication record.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B JB_API_KEY
API key for the language model endpoint.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
Fallback API key if
.B JB_API_KEY
is not set.
.TP
.B JB_SESSION
The current session's uuid \(em set by
.B jb run
and inherited by child processes.  Resolved as
.B @
by the metadata verbs.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration directory.  Defaults to
.BR $HOME/.config .
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Directory for temporary files (bash output exceeding limits).
Defaults to
.BR /tmp .
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/jb/config.json
Global configuration file.
.TP
.B .jb/config.json
Local (per-repository) configuration file.
.TP
.B .jb/sessions/<uuid>/session.jsonl
The conversation \(em pi session format v3.
.TP
.B .jb/sessions/<uuid>/events.jsonl
The live event stream \(em pi json-mode, delta-only.
.TP
.B .jb/sessions/<uuid>/metadata.json
Session metadata \(em the jb index.
.TP
.B AGENTS.md
Project context file.  Walked from cwd upward.
.TP
.B .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md
Project-local skill definitions.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.  Final answer printed to stdout.
.TP
.B 1
Error: API failure, session not found/ambiguous, refused commit,
.B JB_SESSION
not set.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown command, missing prompt on stdin, bad arguments.
.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT
Interrupt the run: the assistant entry is recorded with stopReason
aborted and the session closes with status error.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Same as SIGINT.
.TP
.B SIGPIPE
Default disposition (die).
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Initialize and run a session:
.RS
.nf
.B jb init
.B echo "hello" | jb run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Continue from a previous session:
.RS
.nf
.B echo "continue" | jb run --fork 9f3c2a1b
.fi
.RE
.PP
Commit and inspect:
.RS
.nf
.B jb commit 9f3c2a1b
.B jb status
.B jb log --graph
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export the pi viewer and the linear JSONL:
.RS
.nf
.B jb export 9f3c2a1b /tmp/session.html
.B jb export 9f3c2a1b /tmp/session.jsonl
.fi
.RE
.PP
Tail the live event stream:
.RS
.nf
.B tail -f "$(jb path 9f3c2a1b)/events.jsonl"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Print version:
.RS
.B jb --version
.RE
.PP
Read this manual page from within a jb session:
.RS
.B man jb | col -b
.RE
.
.SH BUGS
.B jb
has no known bugs.  See events.jsonl for details.
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR col (1),
.BR pi (1)
